content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Pilot",
      "description": "Certified flight crew member responsible for operating an aircraft."
    },
    {
      "name": "Flight Plan",
      "description": "Operational document defining aircraft, crew, route, and timing.",
      "attributes": [
        "Pilot",
        "Aircraft",
        "Flight Attendant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Aircraft",
      "description": "Air vehicle assigned to flights and subject to maintenance.",
      "attributes": [
        "Maintenance Record"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Maintenance Record",
      "description": "Historical log of inspections, repairs, and technical actions on an aircraft."
    },
    {
      "name": "Flight Attendant",
      "description": "Cabin crew member assigned to passenger operations on a flight."
    },
    {
      "name": "Clarification Request",
      "description": "Pilot’s request for operational clarification regarding a flight plan."
    },
    {
      "name": "Irregularity Report",
      "description": "Pilot-submitted report describing a technical irregularity encountered during flight."
    },
    {
      "name": "Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Staff member responsible for crew assignment, aircraft allocation, and operational coordination."
    },
    {
      "name": "Disruption Notice",
      "description": "Notification sent to customer service when operational delays or issues occur."
    },
    {
      "name": "Customer Service Agent",
      "description": "Agent assisting passengers with check-in, rebooking, and baggage issues."
    },
    {
      "name": "Maintenance Engineer",
      "description": "Technician performing aircraft inspections, repairs, and technical assessments."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inspection",
      "description": "Maintenance activity evaluating the condition of an aircraft."
    },
    {
      "name": "Maintenance Extension Notification",
      "description": "Alert indicating that an aircraft requires extended maintenance time."
    },
    {
      "name": "Passenger",
      "description": "Traveler using flight services."
    },
    {
      "name": "Rebooking Options",
      "description": "Possible alternative travel arrangements offered to passengers."
    },
    {
      "name": "Check In",
      "description": "Process of registering a passenger for a flight and issuing travel documents."
    },
    {
      "name": "Baggage Services",
      "description": "Unit responsible for handling, locating, and forwarding passenger luggage."
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Maintenance": {
      "objects": [
        "Irregularity Report",
        "Maintenance Engineer",
        "Inspection",
        "Aircraft",
        "Maintenance Record",
        "Maintenance Extension Notification"
      ]
    },
    "Passenger Affairs": {
      "objects": [
        "Customer Service Agent",
        "Passenger",
        "Check In",
        "Rebooking Options",
        "Baggage Services"
      ]
    },
    "Flight Planning": {
      "objects": [
        "Operations Coordinator",
        "Flight Plan",
        "Pilot",
        "Aircraft",
        "Flight Attendant",
        "Clarification Request",
        "Disruption Notice"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- In case an object appears in multiple bounded contexts, suggest a name change.
- Also suggest a name change if the meaning of the object is too similar to an object from another bounded context
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
